Syntax: tailor <item> <race>

Tailor cuts a piece of clothing or soft armor to fit another body.  Letting
a piece out needs cloth of its own material to let it out with; taking one
in leaves clippings.

Those clippings are not nothing.  They carry every stat the piece carried,
though never its armor, and they can be woven back into thread or handed to
a mage who knows what to do with them.

Metal is a smith's work, not a tailor's.  See FORGE RESIZE.

See also: WEAVE, SEW, FORGE
